1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,759
How many sheets do you actually need?

2
00:00:02,759 --> 00:00:06,562
Most people divide the total
area by the area of a sheet.

3
00:00:06,562 --> 00:00:08,631
Here's why that comes up short.

4
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:12,793
This is a kitchen carcass job on 8×4 MDF.

5
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:14,761
The area sum says 2 sheets.

6
00:00:14,761 --> 00:00:16,934
Nested properly, it needs 3.

7
00:00:16,934 --> 00:00:20,125
Order 2, and you're a
sheet short on the day.

8
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:25,498
Put in your own sheet size, your blade's
kerf, and what you pay per sheet.

9
00:00:25,498 --> 00:00:28,821
Tap a standard size to compare, like 10×4.

10
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:31,611
Using veneered or woodgrain board?

11
00:00:31,611 --> 00:00:36,711
Untick “Parts can turn”, and every panel
keeps the grain running the same way.

12
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:42,201
When you're happy, open the job in the full
app, for cut sheets, labels and quotes.

13
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:47,936
The calculators are free, with
no sign up, at cutnest.co.uk.
